FORENSIC NECROMANCY: IFCOMP EDITION

There are four builds of the game included in this zip file.

web/ has the most user-friendly version, which can be played in a web browser; double-click index.html to start. Unless you have a strong reason to use one of the other versions, this is the one you should play. It looks the best and is the easiest to play, with hyperlinks and a graphical map.

zmachine.z5 is a Z-machine version, for people who prefer to use a dedicated interpreter. This version doesn’t have clickable links or a custom color scheme, but can be played on all sorts of platforms. And it does have better styling than the retro versions: colors for highlighting, italics for emphasis, and so on.

commodore64/ has a Commodore 64 disk image, for retro enthusiasts. Don’t use this one if you’re at all in a hurry—every turn takes several seconds to complete, for the true 1980s experience! This version does not automatically show the map every turn, since it is so slow to draw; type MAP whenever you want to see it.

apple2/ has an experimental Apple II disk image, for a different subset of retro enthusiasts. This one can run faster than the Commodore 64 version, and the screen can hold more characters (with an 80-column card), but it has no text styling at all—so no italics for emphasis, and no distinction between tutorial messages, block quotes, and game text. Sometimes sacrifices must be made for maximum compatibility.

If you run into any problems, ping @Draconis on the forums, or send an email to <dsdraco7@gmail.com>.

Have fun!
